// Title: Tap Installer Execution
// Sigma ID: 99793437-3e16-439b-be0f-078782cf953d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Daniil Yugoslavskiy, Ian Davis, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2023-12-11
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, T1048
// Description: Well-known TAP software installation. Possible preparation for data exfiltration using tunneling
//   techniques
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate OpenVPN TAP installation
// References:
//   - https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/wiki/ManagingWindowsTAPDrivers
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_tapinstall_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\tapinstall.exe" and (not(((FolderPath contains ":\\Program Files\\Avast Software\\SecureLine VPN\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Program Files (x86)\\Avast Software\\SecureLine VPN\\") or FolderPath contains ":\\Program Files\\OpenVPN Connect\\drivers\\tap\\" or FolderPath contains ":\\Program Files (x86)\\Proton Technologies\\ProtonVPNTap\\installer\\")))
